  "differences_and_limits": [
    "Different atomic kernels: escape uses Kramers g_bf=1 plus Milne, approximate collisional ionization, a finite high-shell collision closure, and no n=3 l-mixing. Cloudy has level-dependent atomic data and n=3 l-mixing. This is external-model adequacy evidence, not same-equations solver verification.",
    "Same principal state topology: resolved 1s,2s,2p,3s,3p,3d and collapsed n4/n5; topoff disabled. Cloudy raw H[:] output pads unused states with zeros.",
    "Pure H, no molecules, prescribed T = 9000 K and nH = 1e12 cm^-3. Thermal energy is deliberately not balanced because temperature is fixed.",
    "Blackbody dilution .025 sets4pi integral J=4W sigma T^4. The slab is1e-4cm; halved-thickness test changes neither n2 nor n3 at saved precision. Relevant Lyman line tau~2e-6 and ground continuum tau~1e-10; very low-radio free-free optical depth need not be small.",
    "Final continuum resolution scale .05; .1\u2192.05 changes n2/n3 by about0.1%, smaller than the preregistered5% target.",
    "Cloudy n3s:n3p:n3d is near 1:3:4.77; escape is near 1:4.25:1.04. Missing n3 l-mixing is a motivated candidate, not a demonstrated sole cause of the discrepancy.",
    "The5% n3 agreement target fails for both nmax4 and nmax5. Keep this counterevidence and do not infer physical accuracy from passing numerical tests."
  ],
